@page "/operations"
@attribute [Authorize(Policy = "CustomerService")]

<PageTitle>Session operations | eShop</PageTitle>
<div class="page-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">SESSION OPERATIONS</span><h1>Keep the work. Release the resources.</h1><p>This HTTP-only view observes the same customer-service process without opening its own circuit.</p></div></div>
<section class="panel" data-operations>
    <div class="operations-metrics">
        <div><span>Connected circuits</span><strong data-metric="connected">...</strong></div>
        <div><span>Live circuits</span><strong data-metric="live">...</strong></div>
        <div><span>Context loads</span><strong data-metric="contextLoads">...</strong></div>
        <div><span>Process ID</span><strong data-metric="processId">...</strong></div>
    </div>
    <p class="muted">Single-process diagnostics, not a capacity benchmark. Disconnected circuits may remain retained briefly; watch the live count fall after pause completes.</p>
    <div class="operations-actions">
        <button class="button" type="button" data-presenter-action="drain">Request circuit pause</button>
        <button class="button secondary" type="button" data-presenter-action="shutdown">Stop this service gracefully</button>
    </div>
    <p class="notice subtle" data-operation-status role="status">Connecting to session metrics...</p>
    <p>After stopping, restart <strong>customerservice</strong> in the Aspire dashboard, then resume the original workspace tab. Keep that tab open: a full refresh discards browser-held recovery state.</p>
    <a href="/returns/48021?continuity=true">Open Alex's resolution workspace</a>
</section>
